# Golden records are length-prefixed byte blobs: the 4-byte length in each
# record header and the byte-exact dump/object hashes make any CRLF conversion
# corrupt the baseline.  Keep them byte-for-byte on checkout and commit.
selfhost/golden/** -text

# H9.5: the bootstrap seed is a binary artifact; never normalise its bytes.
selfhost/bootstrap/ivy-stage0.exe -text

# H9.6: the golden baseline is frozen against LF fixture sources.  Some fixtures
# print the bytes between two token positions (multi-line raw strings), so a
# checkout that converted them to CRLF would change the expected output.  Pin
# the corpus (and the std modules the corpus imports) to LF on every platform.
selfhost/corpus/** text eol=lf
std/** text eol=lf
